BCP729-Strathearn Crescent. Elevation Elevation 659.427 m 6 CM BGL, LANDSCAPED
</groundspeak:encoded_hints>
      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="684645625">
          <groundspeak:log_wpt lat="53.537683" lon="-113.461917" />
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="11091667">WillowZilla</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP729 - Strathearn Crescent&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lots of construction in the area, all sorts of survey flagging and lathed off divots in the ground.  I had the GPS on the seat next to me and stopped at 2 spots that turned out only to be pins before smartening up and following the gps.  Surprisingly to me, the cap location was unmarked :P &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684646250">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="946600">Black Shark</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP729 Strathearn Crescent&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There was a lot of construction to get around or through in the area and we wondered if the cap would be plainly marked.  We parked beside an open grassy area full of utility flags and one lathe with ribbon.  Bingo!  But the GPSs wouldn't let us have anything to do with it and steered us closer to the edge of the bank and a great valley view!  We could also catch a bit of the breeze which was very welcome under the hot sun.  This ebony beauty was quickly found seemingly uninvolved in the construction.  Thanks for the cap and the view, ofth.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684152685">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3854161">Stonagal</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP729 - Strathearn Crescent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Got here just before a huge tour(?) group came up and stopped for quite a while. Understandably so - it's a great view from here. Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682475970">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-29T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="4853503">gumbyphv</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;I found BCP729 Strathearn Crescent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After looking for the last two caps, I headed up the hill and stopped by here.  I parked on the street and made the short walk over to the cap while admiring the fantastic view of downtown from here.  Spotted a divot walked over and there was the cap.  Thanks for another great cap with another great view.  TFTBC  &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="674857122">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-03T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3339080">Gimli*/GeoJoce</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP729 - Strathearn Crescent&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There was a recommendation on the Edmonton FB page to come and find this cap as it was in good shape.  I decided to follow that and come and seek it out today after work.  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Like so many others, I'm sure, the news of this cache's archival was almost heartbreaking and just means between now and May 7 there is some finding to do.  :)  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The house I parked next to was huge and for sale!  lol (no thanks)  The view was amazing and the wind was brisk.  I found the cap after a few minutes of nose to the ground.  It was uncovered and in ok shape.  Took my pictures and sat on the bench for a few minutes.  Only a few as the wind was a bit biting up here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On my way home, I tried to find another cap nearby but realized with no tools it would be a no go (I gave it my best).  This one was good for today.  TFTC OFTH and for your years of work with this cache.  So sorry to see it go.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
      <groundspeak:travelbugs />
    </groundspeak:cache>
  </wpt>
